  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759097,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 10 Years HVSC: A Chronicle of Repression (Commodore 64)\n\nTen years have passed since Winston Smith’s rebellion. Oceania remains under the iron grip of the Party, but the seeds of dissent haven't been entirely extinguished. *10 Years HVSC* plunges you into this bleak future as a nameless operative, a new recruit within a clandestine resistance movement struggling to survive in the shadows.\n\nThis challenging platformer for the Commodore 64 delivers a stark and unsettling experience, mirroring the oppressive atmosphere of Orwell’s *1984*. Navigate treacherous environments – crumbling apartment blocks, surveillance-laden streets, and the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police – while evading patrols and disabling surveillance systems. \n\nGameplay focuses on precise jumps, strategic use of limited resources (like brief moments of electronic interference to disable cameras), and avoiding detection.  Discover hidden messages and fragments of information that reveal the true extent of the Party’s control and the dwindling hope for freedom.  *10 Years HVSC* isn't just a game; it's a chilling reminder of the fragility of liberty and the enduring power of totalitarianism."
    },
